Just before the Castle, statues brought the spells light and detect
monster, and a magic marker on Dlvl21 wrote a +oID.  Back to the stash
for IDing, writing 2 ?oEA (AC-18 now) and set off to storm the castle.
 A few Master Liches made it tricky, but at T27170 he got the 2nd WoW
which went straight to his sack (still no BoH) hopefully for good. 
Having such early luck Bourland felt the need to earn some karma back
from finding the early wand.  The 4 castle dragons left no scales, but
the armory left an alchemy smock and a silver dagger.  The robe was
kept for MC reasons, he was really holding out for Red Scale Mail.

3. Hell - and I mean it

So Hell without FR is one thing, but having no magic mapping added
onto that is rough.  Bourland felt a like a little pacifist, having
his only pet now (Dippy the Green Dragon) lead the way around the
mazes.  He still hit his share of fire traps, and his max HP had
dropped from 146 to 132 by Asmodeus.  Paid off most of the usual
suspects, and by T32059 he recharged my nutrition again and saw a key
boost to lvl17, which meant Teleport Control.

Still without a bag of holding, and thus many stashes, he  invoked the
Eye often to sort and drop off the holy water he was often creating
from the Horn of Plenty.  Alchemy was a proactive solution to fire
traps, and his HP were up to 277.

Anyway, he dealt with Orcus from below, but an Arch Lich summoned a
Red Dragon which left scales.  Now his stash contained Silver, Red,
and Orange scales, just waiting a ?oEA again to make into Mail.  Town
also brought an oilskin bag, which replaced the lowly sack.  Soon the
square was marked T35863 and he began the search for Vlad's tower,
eventually looking *everywhere* from 38-43 for it, even casting light
where he'd been.

I then realized I didn't count the Valley in my calculation, and sure
enough Dlvl37 hadn't been fully mapped. ;)  Armed with "oReflection
and =oSleath he visited the wizard, and still his only means of
levitation was the spell.
Hunger struck again in the Sanctum, and Bourland found himself caught
without reflection at a bad time when a Master Lich and his black
dragon friends devastated his armor (poof to Green Dragon Scale Mail
and robe).  AC at -9 now meant everything was causing some serious
hurt, so he decided to be smarter about choosing my battles.  That
wand of wishing kept talking to me (magic marker, please), but he kept
it hidden from my view deep in the oilskin sack.

Nutrition was recharged again, and this time his Lvl went from 21 to
23!  The amulet was soon his, as was a key =oFA find in a chest. 
After checking all the priest's clothes, the only find was a burnt +2
small shield, which was taken in case the switch from +6 quarterstaff
to silver dagger was made.

4. The climb

The climb was typical, save getting thrown back 5 times in a row into
Orcus town, and featured a *hot* move of accidentally casting stone to
flesh on myself.  Bye bye luckstone and ring of slow digestion! 
Fortunately, he remembered seeing a spare in one of the Orcus shops,
so he went back for it.  The time without the ring made him need to
recharge my hunger again, but this time he saw my level go the other
way, from 23 down to 18 (doh!).

The climb went on, but Dimpy the Green Dragon was ditched because his
eating interfered with his desires to avoid wasting death shots on the
wizard.  Rodney finally appeared in the hallway of the Castle, and
with the /oDeath at (0:3), the third shot did the deed.

At Dlvl21, he learned the need for sleep resistance if your MC is
poor, as a Nazgul rid Bourland of 2 levels in his sleep.  Killing a
poor innocent Gnome put that back to 17 (TC is key), and he finally
made his way back to the final upstairs, and looking at his goods, he
was a ragged character armed with:

