So there I sat, with the Amulet in Bourland's hands, never having been
so unprepared for the Planes.  I thought AC-8 might be suicide, but he
did have some decent wands and the occasional means of recharge.  The
4 "oLS were a good comfort, but i really wanted him to survive.  Still
that WoW was burning in his back pocket and in a moment of weakness I
rationalized that his permanent lightsource was a weight too much, and
he needed a magic marker instead.  One #rub and he had a peaceful
djinni that granted no wish and the RGN was mocking him for being so
weak.  So with a deep breath, and shaky nerves, he put on his Orange
Scales and hit < and went off to surely die.

5. Endgame

With only 3 portal finding scrolls, he decided to be quick on Earth
and hope to randomly find it on Air or Fire.  Earth saw a lot of
dodging followed by a breaking of a /oTel (3:1) to clear the way.

He was not looking forward to Air.  Putting on his "oReflection, and
armed with 12 death shots he took care of the Air Elementals and some
dragons and tried to avoid the damage that many of the vortices also 
gave the intrinsic weak Wizard.  Soon he saw his Power depleted and
the 12 death rays were going too fast.  In all, 2 !oFH were used,
1more /oTel, and while engulfed by an Air Elemental he had to #invoke
the PYEC one more time to find that 13th Death shot.  The portal still
undiscovered, he found himself surrounded and used confused taming to
make some friends and danced to avoid the pounding.

Eventually it was cleared out for the most part and Bourland was
excited to rest and have his Power fill up and maybe even hang out
enough to charge a /oDeath again.  The plan was not to be, as one
faulty step saw him discovering the portal without any of his new
pets, and with Pw:30(242).

In Fire, without FR or pets or taming and few offensive wands, he read
?oGD while confused and found the portal and thunk.  Changing inside a
dust cloud, he tried to make Pw go up and use ?oFH when needed.  He
waited until he was seriously surrounded and broke another (2nd to
last) /oTel, and made a mad dash to the portal and had a good 10 turns
to prepare.  Checking the Turn counter, he recharged a /oDeath, and
then swapped to Orange scales again, although Silver got some
consideration.  To buy time, he swapped conflict and free action to
spend as much time as possible to make the next invocation sooner. 
Naturally, a balrog threw a potion of sleeping on him during this
process, so he was forced to once again 2nd guess his armor choice. 
Off to go to the Water Plane after putting free action back on, and he
went with the choice of robe/orange/"oLS over smock/red/"oR and hoped
for no poisoning.

I hate the Water Plane, and I'm really claustrophobic and hate the
bubble and those little ; things.  Magic Missile was fired whenever
they were within range, and when it was totally surrounded by E's he
had to break the last /oTel, a decision made easier by me thinking he
had a nice /oTel(0:8) in my bag for the Astral.  Sadly, it was digging
instead he would later find out.  Anyway, I made a dash for the ^
ignoring a bag floating by which may have been holding, but at this
point it didn't matter.

6. Astral 

So, there stood Bourland, devoid of Power, no Poison Resistance, no
Reflection, 1 !oFH, no /oTel, 3 death charges, and an AC of -8. 
Famine was to the left (thought best to avoid since foodless),
Pestilence to the middle, and Death to the Right.  On the way to
Death, he dealt with two Master Liches, and then Death was waiting for
him near the door, and Pestilence already walking over.  A +6 dagger
requires some hits, and soon enough the deadly touch was withering
Bourland away.  he tried to line up 3 priests in a row for one death
shot, and canceled the yellow dragon's breath weapon.  Finally making
it through the doorway, he used cursed genocide to make blue jellies
be a nice barrier.  By the time he could maneuver around the mess, the
Yellow Dragon was putting on a beating, so the last !oFH was quaffed.

He entered the outer temple area, and the priests were really putting
on the hurt.  He canceled a Red Dragon, and used (what he thought
were) his last two death rays to take out 6 priests.  He finally made
it to the doorway with only a few priests in the way, and at that
moment the Hunger status appears and the HPs drop below 100.  Down to
one Priest and his insects blocking the way, his options were zapping
a /oFire, recharging a death wand (probably 25 turns too early),
dropping the amulet and casting Magic Missile.  After doing some
calculations, he just started whacking away.  After four attacks and
down below 60 HPs, the road was clear to the altar.  Exhausted and not
even wanting to think about the return trip, he walked up the altar
with priests charging behind and he hit the : key and stopped in
disbelief as the altar was Neutral.  Without hesitation, the Amulet
was offered, and a demigod was made.

